---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";

const crumbs = [{ name: "Home", path: "/" }, { name: "Disclaimer" }];
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="HomeDIYCalc disclaimer: calculator results are estimates only. Confirm quantities with your supplier and a qualified professional for structural work."
  canonical="/disclaimer/"
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-4xl">Disclaimer</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: November 23, 2026.</p>
  <div class="mt-6 max-w-3xl space-y-4 text-slate-700">
    <p>
      The calculators on HomeDIYCalc produce <strong class="text-slate-900">estimates</strong>,
      not guarantees — not guaranteed purchase quantities, and not professional
      engineering advice. Please read this disclaimer before relying on any result.
      HomeDIYCalc is operated by an individual, not a company.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Results depend on your inputs</h2>
    <p>
      A calculator can only be as accurate as the measurements and values you enter. A
      mismeasured wall, an incorrect depth, or a coverage rate that does not match the
      product you actually buy will change the result. Measure carefully and double-check
      your numbers.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">What calculators cannot account for</h2>
    <p>
      Calculators do not account for site conditions such as slope, uneven ground,
      compaction, spillage, damaged or defective material, cutting waste beyond the
      allowance you set, or local building codes and permit requirements. Waste allowances
      and coverage rates are adjustable for exactly this reason — set them to match your
      job and your products.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Costs are your prices, not ours</h2>
    <p>
      Cost estimates appear only when you enter prices, and they use the prices you
      entered. The site supplies no prices of its own. Actual prices vary by supplier,
      location, and time — confirm them before ordering.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing on this site is engineering, architectural, or construction advice. For
      structural work, load-bearing changes, electrical or plumbing work, or anything
      governed by a building code, consult a qualified professional.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-bold text-slate-900">Your responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      Always confirm final quantities with your supplier before ordering, and allow extra
      material for your specific conditions. HomeDIYCalc is not responsible for
      over-ordering, under-ordering, or any cost or delay that results from using an estimate.
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
